    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d482-a1">

                <pb facs="1051" n="955" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg955"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No 196—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Duke of Tetuan to Mr.
                            Lowell.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-31"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 31,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>; I have the honor to make known to
                    your excellency, referring to the affair which occasioned your note of the 30th
                    December last, as to the arrival at Manila of the vessels Bullion, Frank
                    Lambeth, Washington, Henry A. Litchfield, and Stephen, that the minister of
                    ultramar informs me that he has ordered the restitution of the additional sum
                    collected from the consignees of said vessels by exacting tonnage dues according
                    to the number of Spanish tons, instead of those which appeared in the register
                    of each vessel.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this opportunity to reiterate to your excellency the assurance
                    of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Duke of</hi> TETUAN.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
